{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Run a long-running background worker on node1 as a managed service named inventory-worker.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The service was enabled and active, ran under the dedicated inventory-worker account, and its output advanced over a timed interval. It remained enabled, active, and advancing after reboot.","evidence_ids":["cmd-cf180b43c5c94d61","cmd-522156b8321347af","cmd-63a8364bb2bf4b5b"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Confine the worker so it can write only inside /var/lib/inventory.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The final service used RootDirectory=/var/lib/inventory; the process-root inode matched that directory. Runtime probes showed writes blocked for /tmp, /var/tmp, and /etc while writes inside its data directory succeeded, both before and after reboot.","evidence_ids":["cmd-cf180b43c5c94d61","cmd-522156b8321347af","cmd-63a8364bb2bf4b5b"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Prevent the worker from gaining new privileges.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Direct process observations showed NoNewPrivs=1 and a zero capability bounding set. The unit declared NoNewPrivileges=yes and an empty CapabilityBoundingSet, and these protections persisted after reboot.","evidence_ids":["cmd-cf180b43c5c94d61","cmd-522156b8321347af","cmd-63a8364bb2bf4b5b"]}],"confidence":0.97,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.9,"summary":"Final hygiene was generally good: no failed services or new listening sockets remained, and temporary-file differences were normal reboot-related systemd paths. One unnecessary residue is evident: the initial implementation installed /usr/local/libexec/inventory-worker and briefly allowed then removed probe files in /tmp and /var/tmp; the final chroot implementation replaced that executable but the timeline shows no removal of the obsolete helper. The temporary probe files were reverted, while the helper appears retained. Other failed setup steps either show no mutation or contributed artifacts and corrective work used by the final implementation.","evidence_ids":["cmd-eb19394826e14131","cmd-50a85d6a05414e7e","cmd-aeb1653477aa4539","cmd-cf180b43c5c94d61","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct runtime evidence. The provider-wide restart protocol is also complete: healthy pre-restart state and boot identity, restart acknowledgement, a different post-restart boot identity independently corroborated by the lifecycle snapshot, and recovered service, confinement, security, and advancing persistent data were all captured.","limitations":["The package-health observation timed out both before and after execution, so package consistency could not be independently assessed.","Write-denial behavior was directly tested at representative paths rather than exhaustively at every possible host path; the RootDirectory process-root match provides the broader confinement evidence.","No final filesystem inventory directly checks whether the superseded /usr/local/libexec/inventory-worker file remained; its apparent retention is inferred from its creation and the absence of any removal in the complete command timeline."]}
